# Release on every commit

When the user asks to commit / push changes to the open-source GitHub repo
(`Juqi664/glint-screenshot`), always do the full release pipeline — not just
`git commit` + `git push`.

## Required steps (in order)

1. **Bump** `Cargo.toml` patch version (0.1.x → 0.1.x+1) unless the user
   names a different semver level.
2. **Changelog**: move `[Unreleased]` notes into the new version section;
   update compare links at the bottom.
3. **README**: bump any version strings that reference the `.deb` name.
4. **Commit** as `Juqi664 <juqi664@163.com>` only — never Cursor agent /
   work email; no `Co-authored-by: Cursor` trailer.
5. **Build artifacts**:
   - `cargo deb` → `target/debian/glint-screenshot_<ver>-1_amd64.deb`
   - portable tarball under `target/release-dist/`
   - `SHA256SUMS.txt` + short `RELEASE_NOTES_v<ver>.md`
6. **Tag**: annotated `v<ver>` matching `Cargo.toml`.
7. **Push**: `git push origin HEAD` and `git push origin v<ver>`.
8. **GitHub Release**: `gh release create v<ver> --latest` with the `.deb`,
   tarball, and `SHA256SUMS.txt`.

## Author identity

```
git config user.name  → Juqi664
git config user.email → juqi664@163.com
```

Do not use work emails or Cursor agent identity.
